Because XOR is an isometry, binding a whole set of vectors with the same key moves them all without changing any distance between them. That is how a role attaches to a value without destroying the grading between neighboring values, and it is why the encoder can bind first and bundle afterwards.
Permute
is a cyclic rotation of the entire D-bit string. Rotating a hypervector produces something unrelated to the original, which is exactly what is wanted: it is how position in a sequence is marked, so that the same three bars in a different order become a different vector.
