Bundle
is the superposition operator, and it is the only one that is not exactly invertible. It takes an element-wise majority: for each of the D bit positions, count how many inputs have a one there and take whichever wins. The result is similar to every input and unrelated to everything else, and the implementation goes through a signed accumulator so that weights are possible:
