A row is labeled UP or DOWN by the sign of the forward return over the horizon, but only when that move clears
k * sd * sqrt(horizon)
. The
sd * sqrt(horizon)
part is the move a random walk of that length would typically produce, and
k
scales it: the shipped value is 0.5, so a row has to travel half of a typical walk before it earns a label. Rows that do not clear it are dropped rather than assigned to a third class, which on the gold sample removes 1199 of 2873 candidate rows and leaves 1674. Dropping them is deliberate: a model that has to separate the flat middle spends all its capacity there.
It is also a choice with a cost, because the filter reads the future. Whether a bar clears the threshold is decided by the five bars after it, so the rows the model trains and is scored on are a subsample selected with information that does not exist when the bar closes. Live, the question the filter asks cannot be asked. Everything measured later is therefore measured on a conditional subsample: given that a bar did not stay inside the flat band, how well is its direction classified. That is a legitimate question, and not the same question as how well the model would do pointed at every bar.
The library offers no abstain rule to close that gap, and it should be clear that the margin band is not one. The section on the band shows why: for a fitted model the band is not a significance test, and a two-class model with the flat rows removed always answers UP or DOWN. A causally available rule for when not to act is left to the caller, and it is the first thing anyone building on this would have to add.
Now the encoding. A bar becomes a
record
: each feature is quantized to a level, the level is bound with that feature's role vector, and the six results are bundled. Binding first stops the six from being confused with each other; bundling second keeps the record graded, so a bar that is a little different produces a record that is a little different. A window of bars becomes a
sequence
: each record is rotated by its distance from the newest bar and all of them are XORed together.
