The rotation is what turns a bag of bars into a sequence, and the test measures it rather than asserting a threshold. Reversing three bars moves the sequence by 1658 bits of 4096, while changing one bar in the middle moves it by 424. The claim checked is the relative one, because the heuristic that unrelated vectors sit near D/2 apart belongs to random vectors, and a record is a bundle of bound levels.
One detail in
SetRangesFrom
is worth calling out. Quantizer bounds are taken from training rows only, and both tails are trimmed by two percent before the range is set. Without the trim, one outlier bar sets the range and every ordinary bar lands in the same level, producing a codebook that is technically correct and completely uninformative.
