Cross-checking a numerical library against another implementation usually means agreeing to some tolerance, and the tolerance is a judgment call. Here it is not, because there is no floating point in the pipeline. Bind is XOR, bundle is an integer majority, similarity is a population count, and learning is an integer add. The only float in the library is the final division by D for display.
